From e5cec57c596213683f24b39b29573fc05349e9c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alantero <36408154+alantero@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:40:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Keep the Vulkan pipeline cache across sessions on macOS

On MoltenVK a new pipeline translates its SPIR-V to Metal Shading Language
and compiles it, tens to hundreds of milliseconds. The graphics pipelines
now share a VkPipelineCache, read from the cache folder
(native-vulkan-pipelines.bin) when the first pipeline is created and
written once none has been created for a few seconds and at shutdown. A
pipeline seen in an earlier session is then created in a few milliseconds
(Metal keeps its own compiled code by source).

Elsewhere the drivers keep their own caches, and nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
